# Rename this file as harbour-ferry.changes to include changelog
# entries in your RPM file.
#
# Add new changelog entries following the format below.
# Add newest entries to the top of the list.
# Separate entries from eachother with a blank line.

# * date Author's Name <author's email> version-release
# - Summary of changes

* Tue Jul 07 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.7.0-1
- Encrypted libraries (FR-04): password prompt on first access, key kept
  in Sailfish Secrets, lock icons, works for browsing and sync pairs
- Sync conflict detection with notification (FR-12)
- First start opens the account setup automatically (wizard)
- German translation (DEV-03)
- Ship rclone MIT license notice (PK-04); polished package description

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.6.2-1
- Timer: switch to OnCalendar with Persistent=true so runs missed during
  device suspend are executed on wake-up (monotonic timers stall asleep)
- Paused pairs now show a "Paused - long-press to resume" hint

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.6.1-1
- Fix crash on non-ASCII paths (umlauts): subprocess argv now UTF-8 encoded
- Fix --max-delete getting a float value from the settings slider
- Fix background timer: 5-minute interval added to the timer manager
- Account and settings pages are dialogs now (accept at the top right)
- Sync list: folder names instead of full paths, target + last-run date in
  the second line; header spacing; auto-refresh picks up background runs
- 2FA accounts: explain that a login token is stored instead of a password

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.6.0-1
- UI: tab bar on the main page (local syncs / remote), three-line sync
  list with last-run timestamp, account password visible in settings,
  two-line account summary
- M4b: systemd timer wiring with interval setting (FR-18), network rule
  with skip banner (FR-19/FR-19a), safety-abort confirm + force run
  (FR-14/FR-14a), failure notifications (FR-20), editable exclude
  patterns + max-delete setting (FR-15), cover status + sync action
- Timer helper now runs the real sync engine headless

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.5.0-1
- Remote browser: View for .txt and images, plain text Edit for .txt
- M4a: sync pairs (folder/single file) with editor, own pickers (FR-10)
- bisync engine with required flag set, resync on first run, max-delete
  safety, conflict-resolve newer, serial runs (FR-11..FR-17)
- New main page: local syncs list with live status; remote libraries
  attached via swipe (section 5.1); per-pair sync log viewer (NFR-04)

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.4.1-1
- Fix app hang: rclone no longer prompts interactively for the config
  password (--ask-password=false on every invocation)
- Fix secrets lockout when mixing SDK-debugger and app-grid launches:
  new collections use NoAccessControlMode; existing collection is migrated
  once (non-destructively) when access works; clear error message otherwise

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.4.0-1
- M3: upload via own file browser with multi-selection (FR-06, OD-08);
  restricted to standard user folders + removable media (AD-07c)
- In-app banner feedback (Notices) for download/upload/delete/new folder
- Sequential multi-file upload with per-file progress and cancel

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.3.0-1
- M2: Sailfish Secrets integration over the P2P D-Bus socket (AD-04);
  config password migrated automatically from the M1 file store
- Remote browser: list libraries/folders, navigate, download to
  ~/Downloads with progress + cancel, delete with remorse, create folders
  (FR-05, FR-07, FR-08, FR-09 basics)
- Diagnostics: Secrets store/get roundtrip test

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.2.0-1
- M1: account setup with backend-generated form (FR-01/FR-01a)
- rclone config manager: non-interactive state machine incl. 2FA (FR-02),
  encrypted rclone.conf (AD-04, interim file-based config password)
- Connection test with friendly error messages (FR-03)
- Settings page; diagnostics moved under Settings (FR-21)
- Diagnostics: Secrets D-Bus introspection dump (input for M2)
- Build: automatic per-arch rclone binary selection (armv7hl/aarch64/i486)

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.1.2-1
- Reload user systemd units after install/upgrade (%post scriptlet)
- Diagnostics run daemon-reload before starting the sync service

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.1.1-1
- Sailjail disabled per AD-07d after TS-00 spike results (OD-11)
- systemd unit runs the helper without sailjail wrapper
- Diagnostics: sandbox-aware probes, UTF-8-safe IO, QML module probes

* Mon Jul 06 2026 domi300 <domi300@gmx.de> 0.1.0-1
- M0 walking skeleton (TS-00 validation build)
- Built-in diagnostics page running the spike tests (FR-21)
- Sailjail profile with explicit permission set (AD-07)
- systemd user service + timer with sailjail-wrapped sync helper (AD-03)
- Backend plugin skeleton with Seafile definition (AD-09)
- Packaging prepared for bundled rclone binary (PK-01)
